# PPPoE Load Balancer Examples
#
# This directory contains example configurations for the ng_pppoe_lb
# (PPPoE Load Balancer) netgraph node.
#
# For detailed documentation, see ng_pppoe_lb(4).

# Prerequisites
# -------------
# Before using these examples, ensure the required kernel modules are loaded:
#
#   kldload netgraph
#   kldload ng_ether
#   kldload ng_pppoe
#   kldload ng_pppoe_lb
#
# Or add to /boot/loader.conf:
#   netgraph_load="YES"
#   ng_ether_load="YES"
#   ng_pppoe_load="YES"
#   ng_pppoe_lb_load="YES"

# Files in this directory
# -----------------------
# basic_2workers		- Basic setup with 2 worker nodes
# basic_4workers		- Setup with 4 worker nodes (multi-core)
# governor_auto		- CPU governor enabled for auto-scaling
# monitor_example	- Example monitoring commands
# pppoe_lb_test.sh	- Comprehensive test script with auto-scaling
# _ngctl_pppoe_lb	- Bash completion for ngctl pppoe_lb commands
# _pppoed			- Bash completion for pppoed

# Shell Completions
# -----------------
# Bash completions (for bash-completion port):
#   sudo cp _ngctl_pppoe_lb /usr/local/etc/bash_completion.d/
#   sudo cp _pppoed /usr/local/etc/bash_completion.d/
#   exec bash  # Reload bash to activate completions

# Tcsh completions (FreeBSD default shell):
#   cp ngctl.completion ~/.cshrc
#   cp pppoed.completion ~/.cshrc
#   source ~/.cshrc

# Testing
# -------
# To test these configurations:
# 1. Load required kernel modules
# 2. Choose a configuration below
# 3. Review and modify interface names as needed
# 4. Run ngctl -f <config-file>

# For comprehensive integration tests (run in VM only):
#   cd tests/netgraph
#   sudo ./ng_pppoe_lb_vm_test.sh

# Auto-Scaling with pppoed
# -------------------------
# pppoed supports automatic worker scaling via CPU governor:
#   pppoed -L -w 2 -G 0 -M 2 -I 5 -c 80 -C 30 em0
#
# Options explained:
#   -L              Enable load balancer mode
#   -w 2            Start with 2 workers
#   -G 0            Governor max workers (0=auto-detect CPU cores)
#   -M 2            Governor minimum workers
#   -I 5            Governor poll interval (seconds)
#   -c 80           Scale up when CPU > 80%
#   -C 30           Scale down when CPU < 30%

# See Also
# ---------
# ng_pppoe_lb(4)      - Kernel module documentation
# pppoed(8)            - Daemon documentation
# ngctl(8)             - Netgraph control utility
